- **Button snippet (≈10 lines around the button that triggers `setView('map_edit')` / `setView("mapedit")`):**

```jsx
function NavBar({setView}) {
  return (
    <nav className="card flex" style={{marginBottom:"1rem"}}>
      <button className="nav-link" style={{marginRight:"0.5rem"}} onClick={() => setView("list")}>Personajes</button>
      <button className="nav-link" style={{marginRight:"0.5rem"}} onClick={() => setView("maps")}>Mapas</button>
      {/* Button that switches the view to the map editor */}
      <button className="nav-link" onClick={() => setView("mapedit")}>Crear mapa</button>
    </nav>
  );
}
```

- **`setView` definition / surrounding code:**  
  `setView` is **not a custom function** in this project; it is the state‑setter returned by React’s `useState` hook:

```jsx
function App(){
  // …
  const [view, setView] = React.useState("list");
  // …
}
```

> **Note:** No separate `function setView(...)` is defined in the repository. The `setView` used by the button is the updater function for the `view` state variable. If you were expecting a custom `setView` implementation, it does not exist in the current source.
